    "result_text": "Green across the board. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field on the owner response \u2014 the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an `initials` string property (read-only) to the `Owner` schema, alongside the existing `displayName`. This regenerates the `OwnerDto` with an `initials` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that computes initials from the entity:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n       + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n\nThis mirrors the existing `displayName` computed-mapping pattern, so it flows through every place owners are serialized (`GET /api/owners/{id}`, list, create). The full test suite passes (12 tests, including the new `Cp06Tests.coreComputesInitials` which asserts `J.S.` for \"john\"/\"smith\").",
